1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCHLESWIG-HOLSTEIN.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ....................1.         ADOLF [VII] ([1295/97]-9 Oct 1353, bur Kloster Visbeck).  "Adolfus comes de Schawenboch" exchanged property with the bishop of Minden, with the consent of "Helene uxoris nostre et Adolfi filii nostri
2 CONC ", by charter dated 23 Nov 1298[175].  "Adolphus comes Holtsacie et in Schowenburg" donated property to Ouerenkerken, with the consent of "Helene uxoris nostre, Adolphi, Gerhardi et Erici filiorum nostrorum", by charter dated 5 Ma
2 CONC r 1308[176].  He succeeded his father in 1315 as Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg.  "Juncker Alff, Fruwe Helena unse moder, Gerhardt und Erich, Graven tho Holsten und Schomborch" donated property to Oueren
2 CONC kerken by charter dated 1315[177].  The necrology of Visbeck records the death "VII Id Oct" of "Adolfus comes qui cum fratre suo Gerhardo epo dedit…"[178].  m firstly (Papal dispensation 4o 25 Feb 1301) HEDWIG von Schwalenberg, da
2 CONC ughter of ---.  Pope Boniface VIII issued a dispensation for the marriage of "Adolfi comitis de Schovemburg" and "Hadewigis comitisse de Swartemberg" despite 4o consanguinity dated 9 Aug 1299[179].  m secondly (1322 before 25 Jul)
2 CONC  HEILWIG zur Lippe, daughter of SIMON [I] zur Lippe & his wife Adelheid von Waldeck (-after 5 Mar 1369, bur Kloster Visbeck).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.  Graf Adolf [VII]
2 CONC  & his first wife had three children: 
2 CONT a)         ADOLF [VIII] (-Famagusta 12 Oct 1366, bur Famagusta Franciscan Church).  He succeeded his father in 1353 as Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg. 
2 CONT b)         HEILWIG .  1330. 
2 CONT c)         ADELHEID (-after 1376).  m (1348) HEINRICH Graf von Sternberg [Schwalenberg], son of --- .  1335/1385. 
2 CONT Graf Adolf [VII] & his second wife had eight children: 
2 CONT d)         GERHARD (-at sea Mediterranean 28 Sep 1366).  Thesaurarius at Minden Cathedral 1349/1359, kustos 1353/1361, generalvikar 1355/1361.  Canon at Köln Cathedral 1354.  Administrator of Verden 1356/1357.  Elected Bishop of M
2 CONC inden 1361, installed 1362. 
2 CONT e)         SIMON (-Petershagen [1361]).  Canon at Minden Cathedral 1350/1356.  Canon at Hamburg and Bremen.  Canon of St Gereon at Köln 1354.  He died in a tournament[180]. 
2 CONT f)          OTTO von Holstein-Schauenburg (-after 16 Mar 1404, bur Kloster Obernkirchen).  He succeeded his brother in 1366 as OTTO I Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg. 
2 CONT -        see below.  
2 CONT g)         BERNHARD (-[1398/1403]).  Canon at Minden Cathedral 1353/1361.  Provost at Ohsen 1362.  Provost at Hamburg Cathedral 1363/1398. 
2 CONT h)         HELENA .  Nun at Visbeck 1353.  
2 CONT i)          MECHTILD .  Franciscan nun at Lemgo 1367/1385. 
2 CONT j)          ANNA (-3 Jan 1358).  m ([1346]) as his second wife, JOHANN von Mecklenburg, son of HEINRICH II "dem Löwen" Fürst von Mecklenburg & his second wife Anna von Sachsen-Wittenberg (-[1393 after 28 Mar], bur Strelitz).  He w
2 CONC as created Herzog von Mecklenburg und Fürst by Imperial Order at Prague 8 Jul 1348. 
2 CONT k)         ELISABETH (-before 30 Apr 1411).  [Abbess of Elten 1400.]
2 CONT
2 CONT .........
2 CONT
2 CONT OTTO von Holstein-Schauenburg, son of ADOLF VII Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg & his second wife Heilwig zur Lippe (-after 16 Mar 1404, bur Kloster Obernkirchen).  Provost of St Bonifatius at Hammeln 136
2 CONC 3/1366.  He succeeded his brother in 1366 as OTTO I Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg.  In Grafschaft Sternberg 1377. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (25 Jun 1368) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Braunschweig-Lüneburg, widow of LUDWIG Herzog von Braunschweig, daughter of WILHELM Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg & his second wife Maria --- ([1338/41]-after 16 May 1410). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Otto I & his wife had [six] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ADOLF [X] (-[17 Mar 1425/9 Oct 1426]).  He succeeded his father in 1405 as ADOLF X Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg.  m (contract 18 Aug 1378) HELENE von Hoya, daughter of ERICH [I] Graf von Hoy
2 CONC a in Nienburg & his wife --- (-after 23 Nov 1414).  Graf Adolf [X] & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==a)         OTTO von Holstein (1400-2 Jun 1464, bur Visbeck).  He succeeded his father in 1426 as OTTO II Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg in Schaumburg und Pinneberg. ==
2 CONT ====
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         [HELENE (-after 1446).  Canoness at Vreden 1389, abbess 1446.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         [ELISABETH (-1449 or after).  [Abbess of Möllenbeck 1406/1407.]  Abbess of Wunstorf 1426/1449.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         WILHELM (-[1391], bur Obernkirchen). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         MECHTILD (-5 Aug 1440, bur Münster Überwasserkloster).  Nun at Obernkirchen 1388.  Abbess of Überwasser at Münster 1388. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         HELENA .  Canoness at Elten 1443.  Canoness at Überwasser at Münster. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         [ELISABETH (-after 1425).  m BERNHARD von Dorstadt, son of --- (-before 1425).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         [LUKKARD (-1412 or after).  m LUDOLF [VIII] Herr zu Steinfurt, son of --- (-1421 before 23 Aug).] 
