1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Eduard II von Ostfriesland, Graf=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Edzard II, Count of East Frisia was count of East Frisia, (24 June 1532, in Greetsiel – 1 March 1599, in Aurich) and the son of Enno II of East Frisia and Anna of Oldenburg.
2 CONT * died on March 1, 1599 in Aurich, Ostfriesland, Deutschland(HRR) and was buried on May 13, 1599 in Lambertikirche (St. Lambert Church), Aurich, Aurich, Lower Saxony, Germany. 
2 CONT * During his reign, he came into conflict with the city of Emden. Edzard was a staunch Lutheran while the city of Emden was mostly Calvinistic. In 1595 Emden revolted and, after an intercession by the Calvinistic Dutch Republic, E
2 CONC dzard was forced to accept a large degree of independence from Emden.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Edzard married [https://www.geni.com/profile-3264691 '''Catherine Vasa'''] on October 1, 1559 in Stockholm, Sverige. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Together they had the following children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24529405 Margarethe, Gräfin von Ostfriesland];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24529465 Anna von Ostfriesland, Kurfürstin von der Pfalz, Markgräfin von Baden-Durlach,  Herzo];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24529517 Enno III Cirksena, Graf]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24529645 Johann III, Graf von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531331 Christof, Graf von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531355 Edzard, Graf von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531409 Elisabeth, Gräfin von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531442 Sofie, Gräfin von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531475 Karl Otto, Graf von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-24531504 Maria von Ostfriesland]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-71742078 Gustav,  Graf  von Ostriesland]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/OLDENBURG.htm#EdzardIIdied1599 Project MedLands OLDENBURG]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ENNO von Ostfriesland,''' son of EDZARD I “der Grosse” Graf zu Ostfriesland & his wife Elisabeth von Rietberg (1505-Emden 24 Sep 1540, bur Emden Große Kirche).  He succeeded his father in 1528 as ENNO I Graf zu Ostfriesland. 
2 CONT '''married (Oldenburg 7 Mar 1530) ANNA von Oldenburg-Delmenhorst, daughter of JOHANN [V] Graf von Oldenburg-Delmenhorst & his wife Anna von Anhalt (14 Nov 1501-Greetziel 10 Nov 1575).  Regent 1542-1558, 1561.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Enno II & his wife ANNA von Oldenburg-Delmenhorst had six children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''ELISABETH''' (10 Jan 1531-5/6 Sep 1558, bur Möllenbeck).  m (Aurich 23 May 1555) JOHANN Graf von Holstein-Schaumburg, son of JOBST I Graf von Holstein-Schauenburg & his wife Maria von Nassau-Dillenburg (before 25 N
2 CONC ov 1512-Bückeburg 10 Jan 1560, bur Möllenbeck). 
2 CONT * 2.         '''EDZARD''' (24 Jun 1532-Aurich 27 Feb or 1 Mar 1599, bur Aurich St Lamberti).  He succeeded in 1558 as EDZARD II Graf von Ostfriesland.  '''married  (Stockholm 1 Oct 1559) KATHARINA Pss of Sweden, daughter of GUSTAF
2 CONC  I King of Sweden & his second wife Margareta Eriksdotter [Leijonhufvud] (6 Jun 1539-Berum 21 Dec 1610, bur Aurich St Lamberti).'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Edzard II & his wife KATHARINA Pss of Sweden had eleven children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''MARGARETA''' (Schloß Westerås 22 Nov 1560-Aurich 10 Sep 1588, bur Emden Große Kirche). 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''ANNA''' (Aurich 26/28 Jun 1562-Neuhaus am Elbe, Bohemia 27 Apr 1621, bur Heidelberg Heiliggeistkirche). '''married firstly (Heidelberg 12 Aug 1583) as his second wife,''' LUDWIG VI Elector Palatine, son of FRI
2 CONC EDRICH Pfalzgraf zu Simmern [later Pfalzgraf von Simmern, and later FRIEDRICH III Elector Palatine] & his first wife Maria Markgräfin von Brandenburg-Bayreuth (Simmern 4 Jul 1539-Heidelberg 12 Oct 1583, bur Heidelberg).  '''marrie
2 CONC d secondly (post-nuptial contract Carlsburg bei Durlach 17 Nov 1585) ERNST FRIEDRICH Markgraf von Baden-Durlach,''' son of KARL II Markgräfin von Baden-Durlach & his second wife Anna Pfalzgräfin von Veldenz (Mühlburg 17 Oct 1560-R
2 CONC emchingen 14/24 Apr 1604, bur Pforzheim Schloßkirche).  '''married thirdly (Graben bei Karlsruhe or Grabow, Mecklenburg''' 7 Mar 1617) as his first wife, JULIUS HEINRICH von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of FRANZ II Herzog von Sachsen-La
2 CONC uenburg & his second wife Marie von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel (Wolfenbüttel 9 Apr 1586-Prague 20 Nov 1665, bur Schlakenwerth Gruftkapelle).  '''He succeeded in 1656 as JULIUS HEINRICH Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* c)         '''ENNO''' (30 Sep 1563-Leerort 19 Aug 1625, bur Aurich St Lamberti).  '''He succeeded his father in 1599 as ENNO III Graf von Ostfriesland.''' 
2 CONT >>>>>* d)         '''GUSTAV''' (1565-1608). 
2 CONT >>>>>* e)         '''JOHANN''' (1566-23 Jan 1625, bur Kloster Rietberg).  Graf von Rietberg, de iure uxoris.  m (Rietberg 4 Sep 1601) his niece, SABINA KATHARINA von Ostfriesland Gräfin von Rietberg, daughter of ENNO III Graf von 
2 CONC Ostfriesland & his first wife Walpurgis von Rietberg (Esens 1582-31 May 1618, bur Kloster Rietberg).  Johann & his wife had children: 
2 CONT >>>>>* f)          '''CHRISTOPH''' (1569-Luxembourg 19 Mar 1636).  Canon at Magdeburg 1597/1599.  Herr zu Rumpst und Spontin.  '''married ([13 Aug 1613]) as her second husband, LAMBERTINE de Ligne, widow of PHILIBERT de la Baume M
2 CONC arquis de Saint-Martin,''' daughter of LAMORAL [I] Prince de Ligne & his wife Anne Marie de Melun (22 Jun 1593-14 Feb 1651, bur Spontin).  She married thirdly (contract Spontin 7 Feb 1640) Jean Baptiste de la Baume Marquis de Sain
2 CONC t-Martin. 
2 CONT >>>>>* g)         '''EDZARD''' (1571-1572). 
2 CONT >>>>>* h)         '''ELISABETH''' (b and d 1573). 
2 CONT >>>>>* i)          '''SOPHIA''' (5 Jun 1574-Pewsum 20 Mar 1630, bur Aurich St Lamberti). 
2 CONT >>>>>* j)          '''KARL OTTO''' (1577-Znaim 28 Feb 1603, bur Anrich St Lamberti). 
2 CONT >>>>>* k)         '''MARIE''' (25 Apr 1582-Dannenberg 9 Jul 1616, bur Dannenberg St Johannis).  '''married  (Dannenberg 25 Apr 1613) as his first wife, JULIUS ERNST Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Dannenberg, son of HEINRI
2 CONC CH Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Dannenberg & his wife Ursula von Sachsen-Lauenburg (Dannenberg 10 Mar 1571-Dannenberg 26 Oct 1636, bur Dannenberg St Johannes).''' 
2 CONT * 3.         '''ANNA''' (3 Jan 1534-Heidelberg 20 May 1552, bur Aurich St Lamberti). 
2 CONT * 4.         '''HEDWIG Gräfin von Ostfriesland''' (29 Jun 1535-Harburg 4 Dec 1616, bur Harburg Stadtkirche).  '''married  (contract 3 Oct 1562, 8 Nov 1562) as his second wife, OTTO "der Jüngere" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lünebur
2 CONC g in Harburg, son of OTTO I "der Ältere" Herzog von Braunschweig und Lüneburg in Harburg & his wife Meta van Campe (Celle 5 Sep 1528-20 Oct 1603, bur Harburg Franciscan church).''' 
2 CONT * 5.         '''CHRISTOFFER''' (8 Oct 1536-Ungarn an der Ruhr 13 Sep 1566, bur Emden Große Kirche).  Co-regent 1561.  Canon at Bremen. 
2 CONT * 6.         '''JOHANN [II] der Mittlere''' (20 Sep 1538-Stickhausen 29 Sep 1591, bur Emden Große Kirche).  Co-regent 1566-1591. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
