1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Åbo universitet 1667 Jakob Lang (also Langius) Jacobus Jacobi, Ostrobotniensis 1889 . * In Gävle 1.5.1648. Acting: Oulu customs officer, councilor Jakob Andersson Lang and Kerstin Henriksdotter . Student of Oulu pe
2 CONC dagogy. Student in Uppsala 9 October 1664 Jacobus Jacobi Langius Bothniensis. Get out c. test stretched | Tand. Episc. Lincopiensis. Student in Turku at 1667 [Langius] Jacob. Ostrob _ 90 . The name is copied in the register of the
2 CONC  Pohjalainen department [1667] Jacobus Langius. | Natus Gevaliæ. | Uhloensis Upsaliæ depositus. Philosophiæ et Theologiæ Doctor, imprimis Pastor regimenis. Postea Superintendens Narvensis. et demum Episcopus Lincopensis. \ | 5. Ja
2 CONC cobus Langius, Uhloensis. Upsaliæ depositus. Inskrifven i afdelningen under Mat. Professor Simonis Kexleri Nericiensis third Rectorate, 1667. Doctor of Philosophy and Theology. First Pastor of the Regiment. Later Superintendent in
2 CONC  Narva. Finally Bishop of Linköping diocese. Respondent 23.3.1667 pro exercitio, pr. Axel Kempe 168 . Respondent in Uppsala 3.6.1674 pro gradu, pr. oratory. prof. And. Norcopensis. Student in Oxford 1677. Ordained priest 1683. Pre
2 CONC eses 27.6.1690 pro doctoratu. TT in Turku 3.7.1690. — Secretary to the Swedish High Commissioner Nils Lillieroot in Paris 1678. Secretary to the Ambassador, Baron Nils Bielke there 1680–81. Vicar of Nevanlinna 1683. Superintendent
2 CONC  of the diocese of Ingria in Narva 1688, at the same time vicar of the Swedish parish of Narva. Chief superintendent of Livonia in Riga 1700, at the same time vice-chancellor of the University of Pärnu. Bishop of Tallinn 1701, fle
2 CONC d the war to Sweden 1710. Bishop of the diocese of Linköping 1711. † in Linköping 17.2.1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 1682 Anna Bunge .
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: Chief Military Judge Jakob Lang , nobleman 1716 Lagercreutz U485 († 1756).
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson: Ahvenkoski postmaster, secretary Nils Gustaf Duncan 5889 (born 1731/32, died 1771).
2 CONT
2 CONT Niece's son: Oulu merchant, alderman Abraham Nylander 9646 (born 1779, died 1821).
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother-in-law(?): Skuoritsa vicar Bengt Elgfooth 2837 (born 1680, died 1695).
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother-in-law(?): Jakob Rungius 2904, vicar of Loimaa (born 1681, died 1723).
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother-in-law: Oulu customs officer Johan Mollerus 3765 (born 1691).
2 CONT
2 CONT Son-in-law: Lund University professor Arvid Mollerus , late Moller U495 († 1758).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://ylioppilasmatrikkeli.fi/henkilo.php?id=1889 '''Jakob Lang'''] (''myös'' Langius) Jacobus Jacobi, Ostrobotniensis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Synt. Gävlessä''' 1.5.1648. Vht: Oulun tullinhoitaja, raatimies Jakob Andersson Lang ja Kerstin Henriksdotter. Oulun pedagogion oppilas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ylioppilas''' Uppsalassa 9.10.1664 Jacobus Jacobi Langius Bothniensis. Uloa c. testim. venit. | Tand. Episc. Lincopiensis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ylioppilas''' Turussa kl. 1667. Nimi on kopioitu Pohjalaisen osakunnan matrikkeliin [1667] Jacobus Langius. | Natus Gevaliæ. | Uhloensis. Upsaliæ depositus. Philosophiæ et Theologiæ Doctor, imprimis Pastor regimenis. Postea Sup
2 CONC erintendens Narvensis. et demum Episcopus Lincopensis. \ | 5. Jacobus Langius, Uhloensis. Upsaliæ depositus. Inskrifven i afdelningen under Mat. Professoren Simonis Kexleri Nericiensis tredje Rectorat, år 1667. Philosophiæ och The
2 CONC ologiæ Doctor. Först Regements Pastor. Sedermera Superintendent i Narwa. Slutligen Biskop i Linköpings stift. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Respondentti''' 23.3.1667 pro exercitio, pr. Axel Kempe 168. Respondentti Uppsalassa 3.6.1674 pro gradu, pr. kaunopuh. prof. And. Norcopensis. Ylioppilas Oxfordissa 1677. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Vihitty papiksi''' 1683. Preeses 27.6.1690 pro doctoratu. TT Turussa 3.7.1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ruotsin ylim'''. alilähettilään Nils Lillierootin sihteeri Pariisissa 1678. Lähettiläs vapaaherra Nils Bielken sihteeri siellä 1680-1681. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nevanlinnan''' kirkkoherra 1683. Rovasti s.v. Inkerin hiippakunnan superintendentti Narvassa 1688, samalla Narvan ruots. seurak. kirkkoherra. Liivinmaan pääsuperintendentti Riiassa 1700, samalla Pärnun yliopiston varakansleri. 
2 CONC Tallinnan piispa 1701, pakeni sotaa Ruotsiin 1710. Linköpingin hiippakunnan piispa 1711. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''† Linköpingissä''' 17.2.1716. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pso''': 1682 '''Anna Bunge'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
