1 NAME Axel /Duwall/
2 GIVN Axel
2 SURN Duwall
2 _MARNM Duwall
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1595
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 SEP 1630
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wolgast
3 STAE Mecklenburg-Vorpommern
3 CTRY Germany
1 BURI
2 DATE 13 NOV 1630
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stralsund
3 STAE Mecklenburg-Vorpommern
3 CTRY Germany
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Duwall_nr_241 Adliga ätten Duwall nr 241]
2 CONT * [http://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17729 Axel Duwall]
2 CONT * [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wahl_%28Adelsgeschlecht%29 Adelsgeschlecht Wahl]
2 CONT * F.D.H. Macdowall and William L. MacDougall (2009). The MacDowalls. Clan MacDougall Society of North America, Inc.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Axel Mac-Dougall Duwall died 1630, September 6, in Pommern, Germany. Buried at St. Nicholas' Church, with the king in attendance, 1630, November 13, in Stralsund, Pommern. Appears to have been unmarried. Styled himself "Mag Duwalt
2 CONC ". Held estates in Uppland, Sweden and bought there in 1629: Hallkved in Funbo, Uppland, Sweden. [Hildebrand 1945a]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1624, Captain, Gustaf Horn's regiment.
2 CONT 1626, Major,  brother Jacob's regiment.
2 CONT 1627, March, Poland: Prisoner of the Poles, but was quickly exchanged.
2 CONT 1627, May, Käsemark, Poland: Captured again during a night crossing of the Vistula River, but was freed by early June.
2 CONT 1627, July – 1628, Winter: Dirschau, Poland: Sent with 200 musketeers to assist Lars Kagg, and wintered there.
2 CONT 1628, June, Stralsund, Pommern: Arrived with the first Swedish relief force to the besieged city.
2 CONT 1628, June 27–28, Stralsund, Pommern: Captured during an enemy night attack on the Frauenthor gate.
2 CONT 1628, October, Dömitz, Mecklenburg: Still imprisoned and sought 250 riksdaler for his ransom.
2 CONT 1628, Late, Stralsund, Pommern: Released and helped his brother recruit and train troops.
2 CONT 1629, August, Pillau, East Prussia: On a mission for the king.
2 CONT 1629, Autumn, Sweden: Bought estate: Hallkved.
2 CONT 1630, January, Sweden: Took command of Västerbotten's Regiment.
2 CONT 1630, March, Sweden: King ordered him to prepare his troops for march.
2 CONT 1630, May, Älvsnabben, Sweden: Embarked with the expedition army.
2 CONT 1630, June, Pommern, Germany: Landed and secured the mouth of the Peene River.
2 CONT 1630, July–August, Wolgast, Pommern: Attacked Wolgast, and the town and castle fell on August 14–15. [Hildebrand 1945a]
2 CONT == Research Notes ==
2 CONT * Estimated birth year, birth place. 
2 CONT * Death place Wolgast assumed, but not supported by sources? Hildebrand (1945a) says only Pommern.
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * '''Dähnert 1754:''' ''Pommersche Bibliothek. Dritter Band. Neuntes Stück. Für den September.'' Dähnert, Johann Carl. Greifswald, 1754. S.319-20. [https://www.digitale-bibliothek-mv.de/viewer/fullscreen/PPN774811781_1754/339/ Dig
2 CONC ital Library Mecklenburg-Vorpommern]
2 CONT * '''Elgenstierna 1926:'''  ''Den introducerade svenska adelns ättartavlor. Med tillägg och rättelser. II. af Chapman-Fägerstråle.'' Elgenstierna, Gustaf (red). Stockholm: P. A. Norstedt & Söners Förlag, 1926. S.355. [https://rune
2 CONC berg.org/elgenst/2/0371.html Project Runeberg], [https://litteraturbanken.se/f%C3%B6rfattare/ElgenstiernaG/titlar/%C3%84ttartavlor2/sida/373/faksimil litteraturbanken.se]
2 CONT * '''Hildebrand 1945a:''' "Axel Duwall" in ''"Svenskt biografiskt lexikon (SBL) vol.11"'' p.613. (art av Bengt Hildebrand.), Stockholm: Riksarkivet. hämtad 2026-04-06. https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/artikel/17729 ''"Död:1630-09-06
2 CONC  – Tyskland (i Pommern)", "skrev sig Mag Duwalt", "Synes ha varit ogift"''
2 CONT * '''Hildebrand 1945b:''' "Duwall, släkt" in ''"Svenskt biografiskt lexikon (SBL) vol. 11"'' p. 607.  (art av Bengt Hildebrand.) Stockholm: Riksarkivet. hämtad 2026-04-06. https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/artikel/17727
2 CONT * '''Magin 2016a:''' DI 102, Inschriften Stadt Stralsund, Nr. 345(†) (Christine Magin), in: www.inschriften.net, [https://nbn-resolving.de/urn:nbn:de:0238-di102g018k0034504 urn:nbn:de:0238-di102g018k0034504].
2 CONT * '''Magin 2016b:''' DI 102, Inschriften Stadt Stralsund, Nr. 349† (Christine Magin), in: www.inschriften.net, [https://nbn-resolving.de/urn:nbn:de:0238-di102g018k0034909 urn:nbn:de:0238-di102g018k0034909].
